<title>HONG KONG: Egana Int'l Holdings signs $20 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Egana Int'l Holdings signs $20 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egana International Holding's has signed a US$20 million loan facility, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The facility has a final maturity of three years.</p>
<p>Long Term Credit Bank of Japan is the arranger.</p>
<p>Proceeds are to be used for acquiring &quot;internationally recognised brandnames,&quot; refinancing existing loans and general working capital.</p>
<p>The borrower is a timepiece and jewellery manufacturer.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
